WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.575
The lab runs the guide's own checks in
a test subscription, never production.

2
00:00:04.575 --> 00:00:07.730
The guide has no kit or
developer workbook yet,

3
00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:12.213
so there's no fixture lab; this is
Lab 2, and the authors haven't run it.

4
00:00:12.213 --> 00:00:15.557
You need a test subscription
where someone has applied Step

5
00:00:15.557 --> 00:00:18.500
1 to a pilot management group,
and Reader on that group.

6
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:21.212
Values you supply are in angle brackets.

7
00:00:21.212 --> 00:00:24.981
Step one signs in to the cloud
the subscription lives in

8
00:00:24.981 --> 00:00:28.587
and adds the two Azure C L I
extensions the guide needs.

9
00:00:28.587 --> 00:00:31.937
Step two lists the policy
assignments at the pilot group.

10
00:00:31.937 --> 00:00:34.340
The guide's Validate step says you should

11
00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.813
see the initiatives in
do-not-enforce mode.

12
00:00:36.813 --> 00:00:41.490
Step three lists the platform resources
that need a diagnostic setting:

13
00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:46.636
firewalls, application gateways, Front
Door profiles, key vaults and public I Ps.

14
00:00:46.636 --> 00:00:50.612
Step four takes one of them and
lists its diagnostic settings.

15
00:00:50.612 --> 00:00:54.148
Each should send its logs to
the platform team's workspace;

16
00:00:54.148 --> 00:00:56.860
one with none is a gap
for the platform owner.
